# gap20-100: ~100-body version of gap20.scn (100 bodies, 10x10 block). Generated by gen_legion100.py.
scn 1
# Pinwheel gap, 20 cells (W8 step 0, the audit's `auditgaps` gap 20 alone in its own world): the U-turn's wall
# with a second wall above it (x 98-101, z 0-27), leaving a 20-cell gap (z 28-47). 48 footprint-2 bodies west of the wall are sent to
# a point beyond it; the files must fold into the gap and take it no slower
# than single file. gate.top.files_x100 is the files abreast in the gap strip
# and side.east.t90 the source's rounded90 (90% at x >= 104).
# Speed 1.79999 builds the source's raw 117964 (see uturn.scn).
# Source numbers (main b8a4110, offset 0): see gapsweep.scn (gap 8 = gap 6 for 2x2 bodies; 10: 1314 / 2610 / 4.14;
# 14: 1332 / 2934 / 3.98; 20: 1252 / 2284 / 4.48 as rounded90 / done / files).
name gap20-100
ticks 6000
seed 7
map flat 200 140
wall 98 48 4 92
wall 98 0 4 28
type m mover 2 2500 10 1.79999
gate top 101 0 101 47
line east 104 0 104 140
probe lanes
group A 0 m 100 rect 30 90 60 120 pitch=3
at 1 move A 150 110
